<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Akinyi can make a water-tank stand in <m>{6}</m> days; Otieno can do the same job in <m>{12}</m> days.</p><p>(a) What fraction of the job do they do together in one day? Give a fraction, for example <c>7/12</c>, or a decimal correct to 3 decimal places.</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) How long do they take working together? Give your answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> days  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Add the fractions done in one day, not the times.</p><p>(a) In one day the first does <m>\dfrac{1}{ {6} }</m> of the job and the second does <m>\dfrac{1}{ {12} }</m>. Together:<me>\frac{1}{ {6} } + \frac{1}{ {12} } = {\frac{1}{4}}</me></p><p>(b) The time is <m>1 \div {\frac{1}{4}} = {4}</m> days. This is quicker than the faster one alone, <m>{6}</m> days, as it must be.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>